# .vercelignore — v1.30.7.8 Production Exposure Remediation
#
# Vercel (jadwal-driver-pbsi.vercel.app) auto-deploys this repository as a
# static site on every push to main, with NO framework detection and NO
# prior ignore configuration — it served the entire git-tracked tree,
# including internal engineering/security documentation, verbatim.
#
# firebase.json's own `hosting.ignore` array already establishes this
# project's convention for what must never be publicly served
# (firebase.json, .firebaserc, database.rules.json, firebase-rules.json,
# dotfiles, node_modules, functions/**, docs/**, scripts/**,
# Analytics-V2/**, *.md, package.json, package-lock.json, temp_server.js,
# framework-poc.html). This file mirrors that list — it is not a new
# judgment call, it is applying an already-approved rule to the deploy
# target that was missing it — PLUS several additional directories/files
# confirmed, this session, to be (a) not referenced anywhere in
# index.html or js/app.js's runtime code, and (b) already serving on the
# live Vercel URL: scratch/, "Analytics Export/", "Engineering Operations
# Prototype/", "Petty Cash Center/", legacy/, src/, storage.rules,
# storage-cors.json, database.rules.stageA.json, *.txt.
#
# database.rules.stageA.json is a documented, explicit "ROLLBACK ONLY"
# fully-open rules file (root .read/.write: true) for a break-glass
# scenario — not a secret, but an operational artifact that should not
# be casually public either.
#
# Syntax: same as .gitignore (Vercel's own documented behavior — this
# repo's existing .gitignore is the syntax precedent).
#
# Verified NOT to remove anything index.html/js/app.js/service-worker.js
# actually loads at runtime (see docs/PRODUCTION_SECURITY_DEPLOYMENT_RUNBOOK_v1.30.7.md
# §4/§5 of the v1.30.7.8 remediation for the full CURRENT/TARGET/REMOVED
# file audit this was derived from).

# v1.30.7.8.3 — CRITICAL FIX: every directory-name pattern below is now
# anchored to the repository root with a leading "/". Unanchored gitignore-
# style patterns (e.g. bare "docs/") match a directory of that name at ANY
# depth in the tree, not just the top level. "docs/" was silently also
# excluding js/docs/ — a REAL application code directory (doc-engine.js +
# templates/) that js/app.js statically imports from at its top level. Once
# Vercel started actually honoring this file (v1.30.7.8.2's install/build
# skip fix made that true for the first time — it was previously confirmed
# NOT taking effect at all, see §0.3 of the deployment runbook), that
# collision 404'd js/docs/doc-engine.js on Vercel, which failed js/app.js's
# entire static module graph before a single line of it could run — the
# EXACT documented failure mode from the v1.25.x "Memuat..." hotfix
# (js/config.js's own VERSION_HISTORY), just triggered by a missing import
# instead of a syntax error. The whole application was down on Vercel (the
# URL staff actually use) until this fix. No pattern's INTENDED scope
# changes — every one of these was always meant to mean "the top-level
# directory/file of this exact name," never "anywhere in the tree."

# ── Mirrors firebase.json's hosting.ignore (already-approved convention) ──
/firebase.json
/.firebaserc
/database.rules.json
/firebase-rules.json
/functions/
/docs/
/scripts/
/Analytics-V2/
*.md
/package.json
/package-lock.json
/temp_server.js
/framework-poc.html

# ── Additional gaps found this session, not covered by firebase.json's
#    ignore list either, but equally not required by the running client ──
/scratch/
/Analytics Export/
/Engineering Operations Prototype/
/Petty Cash Center/
/legacy/
/src/
/storage.rules
/storage-cors.json
/database.rules.stageA.json
*.txt

# ── Standard, not project-specific ──
node_modules/
/.firebase/
/firebase-debug.log
/database-debug.log
.env
.env.local
